      "type": "text",
      "text": "I've marked the run anomalous (process-side fault, specific cause unknown) and proposed a test to find the cause.\n\n- **Main sign:** tube pressure stayed at the normal ~3.00 Torr baseline through the heat-up. During growth it has risen steadily: 3.01 → 3.07 → 3.12 → 3.19 → 3.25 Torr, from 2520 s to 3120 s. That's far outside the usual ~0.02 Torr noise.\n- **What's normal:** Ar flow is holding at about 100 sccm and temperature is holding at 750 °C with steady heater power. So the flow controller and the thermocouple don't look like the cause.\n- **Why I can't name the cause:** a leaking seal letting air in and a partly blocked exhaust would both push pressure up like this. The exhaust O2 sensor that would tell them apart isn't installed. That also means the growth stage's own check fails, because nobody can confirm the gas in the tube is clean.\n- **Proposed test:** change the Ar flow and watch how the pressure responds, or close off the pump briefly and watch how fast pressure rises. Either should separate a leak from a blockage.\n\nNo sample has been characterized yet, so there's no evidence either way on whether the material grew. If the run finishes like this, any result shouldn't count as evidence about the recipe."
     }
